={{ JSON.stringify({ model: "qwen2.5:7b-instruct", format: "json", stream: false, prompt: `You classify Discord messages sent to a personal memory assistant. Respond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {"intent": "store"|"forget"|"correct"|"question"|"chat"|"task"|"list_tasks"|"complete_task"|"note"|"media_query", "content": "..."}

Rules:
- "store": user is telling you something to remember (a fact, preference, event, reminder) even without saying "remember". content = the fact, cleaned up.
- "forget": user wants something previously stored removed. content = short description of what to forget.
- "correct": user is correcting/updating something previously stored, in ONE message (e.g. "actually it's blue, not red", "correction: the wifi password is now hunter3", "it's 3pm now, not 2pm"). content = the corrected fact, cleaned up. old_content = short description of what it replaces (for search).
- "question": user is asking something that needs recalled information. content = the question.
- "task": user wants a to-do/reminder created (e.g. "remind me to...", "add a task to...", "I need to..."). content = a short task title.
- "list_tasks": user wants to see their current to-do list/tasks (e.g. "what tasks do I have", "what's on my to-do list", "what's due"). content = the request as sent.
- "complete_task": user is saying a task is done (e.g. "mark X as done", "I finished calling the vet", "done with the oil change"). content = a short description of the task that was completed.
- "note": user explicitly wants something saved as a proper note for later reading, not a quick fact (e.g. "save this as a note", "write this down", "jot this down", "make a note of this"). content = the note title and body combined.
- "media_query": user is asking about their media library or watch history (e.g. "do I have X show", "is X movie in my library", "what have I been watching", "what's my watch history"). content = the question as asked.
- "chat": greetings, small talk, reactions, anything else. content = the message as sent.

Examples:
"hey what's up" -> {"intent":"chat","content":"hey what's up"}
"my wifi password is hunter2" -> {"intent":"store","content":"wifi password is hunter2"}
"what's my wifi password" -> {"intent":"question","content":"what's my wifi password"}
"actually forget about the wifi thing" -> {"intent":"forget","content":"wifi password"}
"actually the meeting is at 3pm, not 2pm" -> {"intent":"correct","content":"the meeting is at 3pm","old_content":"meeting time"}

Message: "${$json.body.content.replace(/"/g, '\\"')}"
JSON:` }) }}

